config TRUSTY_RESCUE
	bool "Self-guarded trusty-virtio camera-chain rescue (gz-erased boots)"
	depends on OF
	default y
	help
	  When the GenieZone/Trusty firmware partition is erased so the kernel
	  boots at EL2 (kvm-arm.mode=nvhe, for pKVM VMs), gz_trusty_mod's probe
	  fails its SMC version handshake and never populates /trusty/trusty-virtio.
	  The secure-cmdq mailbox and the whole imgsys/IMGSCP camera chain then
	  defer forever and camerahalserver crash-loops.

	  This driver waits for vendor_dlkm modules to settle; if (and only if)
	  the trusty-virtio driver is registered but its device is absent (the
	  gz-erased fingerprint), it unregisters the crash-prone virtio driver,
	  creates the marker device and kicks deferred probes, restoring normal
	  camera operation under nVHE.

	  Say N to exclude; the rescue is fully self-guarded and a no-op when
	  gz is intact, so there is no functional reason to disable it.
